  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Liq 505.01 Definitions. As used in this part, unless a different meaning is clearly intended from the text, a \"one-day licensee\" means a holder of a one-day license for voluntary non-profit organizations in order to sell beverages, specialty beverages, and liquor on premises approved by the commission.\n\nSource. (See Revision note at chapter heading for Liq 500) #5043, eff 1-11-91; ss by #6391, eff 11-28-96, EXPIRED: 11-28-04\n\nNew. #8450, eff 10-21-05; ss by #10647, eff 7-24-14; ss by #13461, eff 10-13-22",
